data.value:
• respect the client, their home, their belongings and their environment; The young provider adopts a simple and professional attitude: greet the client, listen to their instructions, stay in the areas provided, do not rummage through or move objects unnecessarily, handle equipment with care, protect the premises during the work, tidy and clean after the mission, report immediately any damage or difficulty, and respect the client’s privacy by taking no photos and sharing no information about what they have seen or heard.
• carry out only the tasks that were accepted and clearly defined before the mission;
• respect the agreed times;
• give prompt notice in case of delay, inability to attend, or difficulty;
• ask for explanations when an instruction is not clear;
• refuse any dangerous, illegal or unplanned task;
• accept constructive feedback after the mission.

• simple gardening: mowing, weeding, collecting leaves;
• tidying a cellar, garage, attic or cluttered room;
• light cleaning: terrace, accessible windows, simple indoor cleaning;
• help with shopping or light carrying of objects;
• help with a light move;
• simple furniture assembly;
• small repairs with no danger;
• simple small painting jobs;
• any other task validated in advance by the platform or the referring coach.

• electrical work, complex plumbing, gas, heating or technical installations;
• work at height, roofs, or use of dangerous machinery;
• personal care, childminding without a specific framework, or transporting people;
• handling of dangerous products;
• any illegal, humiliating, discriminatory task, or any task contrary to the dignity of the person.

If in doubt, the provider must suspend the mission and ask the platform or the referring coach for advice.

• punctuality;
• politeness;
• reliability;
• honesty;
• respect for instructions;
• ability to ask for help;
• care taken with the work;
• respect for the client;
• ability to acknowledge a mistake;
• willingness to learn and to progress.
